# **Kitab-i-Ahdi (The Book of My Covenant)** {#sec-kitab-i-ahd .unnumbered}

## Purpose of Baha'u'llah's Covenant

**1. Original (Persian)**

اگر افق اعلی از زخرف دنيا خاليست ولکن در خزائن توکّل و تفويض از برای ورّاث ميراث مرغوب لا عدل له گذاشتيم گنج نگذاشتيم و بر رنج نيفزوديم ايم اللّه در ثروت خوف مستور و خطر مکنون انظروا ثمّ اذکروا ما انزله الرّحمن فی الفرقان "ويلٌ لکلّ هُمزةٍ لمزة الّذی جمع مالاً وعدّده" ثروت عالم را وفائی نه آنچه را فنا اخذ نمايد و تغيير پذيرد لايق اعتنا نبوده و نيست مگر علی قدر معلوم

**Transliteration**

*Agar Ufuq-i-Aʿlá az zukhruf-i dunyā khālīst, va-lākin dar khazāʾin-i tavakkul va tafwīḍ az barāy-i varathih mīrāth-i marghūb-i lā ʿadl lahu guẕāshtīm. Ganj naguẕāshtīm va bar ranj nayafzūdīm. Aymu'llāh, dar tharvat khawf-i mastūr va khaṭar-i maknūn ast. Unẓurū thumma'udhkurū mā anzalahu'r-Raḥmān fī'l-Furqān: "Waylun li-kulli humazatin lumazatin alladhī jamaʿa mālan wa ʿaddadah." Tharvat-i ʿālam rā wafāʾī nīst. Ānchih rā fanā akhadh namāyad va taghyīr padhīrad, lāyiq-i iʿtinā nabūdih va nīst magar ʿalá qadr-i maʿlūm.*

**Contemporary English**

The Most Exalted Horizon has been free from the ornaments of this world. Yet within the treasuries of trust in God and complete surrender to His will, We have left for the heirs an incomparable inheritance. We left behind no earthly treasure, nor did We add to anyone's burden.

By God! Within material wealth lie hidden fear and concealed danger. Consider this carefully, and remember what the All-Merciful revealed in the *Furqán*: *"Woe to every slanderer and backbiter, who amasses wealth and keeps counting it."* (Qur'an 104:1–2)

The wealth of this world possesses no lasting fidelity. Whatever is overtaken by decay and subject to change has never been, nor is it now, worthy of more than a limited measure of regard.

